    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change follows the patterns already established in this class and codebase:\n\n- The persisted `title` field, its `@Column` mapping, and its getter/setter sit naturally among the other persisted Owner fields, and the schema additions mirror the existing columns across all four dialects.\n- `@Transient public String getSalutation()` is exactly the idiom this class already uses for read-only derived attributes \u2014 `getAgeBand()` and `getIdentityKey()` are the same shape (transient getter, doc comment describing the derivation, no backing column). A maintainer would find it right at home.\n- The derivation logic is small, self-contained, and belongs on the entity next to the data it reads (`title` + `lastName`), consistent with where `getAgeBand()` and `getIdentityKey()` live. Nothing is duplicated and no class/method is turning into a catch-all.\n- The OpenAPI additions (the `title` enum on the request and the read-only `salutation` on the response) match the existing schema style and documentation tone.\n\nPlacing the transient `getSalutation()` immediately after the `title` getter/setter, rather than grouping it with the other transient derivations, is a minor cosmetic choice but reads fine given it's logically tied to the `title` field.",
